      obj: ['Davomiylik va boshlanish nuqtasini for va since bilan ifodalaysiz.', 'You will express duration and starting point with for and since.'],
      ex: ['“for” + muddat: for two years, for a long time, for three hours. “since” + boshlanish nuqtasi: since 2020, since Monday, since I was a child. Ikkalasi ham Present Perfect bilan: I have lived here for ten years = I have lived here since 2015.\nSavol: How long have you lived here? Davom etayotgan holat uchun “stative” fe’llar (know, live, have, be) — I have known him for years (✗ I know him for years). Hozir ham davom etadi!', '“for” + duration: for two years, for a long time, for three hours. “since” + starting point: since 2020, since Monday, since I was a child. Both go with the Present Perfect: I have lived here for ten years = I have lived here since 2015.\nQuestion: How long have you lived here? For states (know, live, have, be): I have known him for years (✗ I know him for years). It continues now!'],
      eg: [['I have lived here for ten years.', 'Men bu yerda o‘n yildan beri yashayman.'], ['She has worked here since 2020.', 'U 2020-yildan beri shu yerda ishlaydi.'], ['How long have you known him?', 'Uni qancha vaqtdan beri bilasiz?'], ['We haven’t seen each other for months.', 'Biz bir-birimizni bir necha oy ko‘rmadik.']],
      w: [['since', '… dan beri', 'с (момента)', 'preposition', 'I have lived here since 2015.', 'Men 2015-yildan beri shu yerda yashayman.', 'sɪns'], ['for', '… muddat', 'в течение', 'preposition', 'I waited for an hour.', 'Men bir soat kutdim.', 'fɔː'], ['duration', 'davomiylik', 'продолжительность', 'noun', 'The duration of the film is two hours.', 'Filmning davomiyligi ikki soat.', 'djuˈreɪʃn'], ['recent', 'yaqinda bo‘lgan', 'недавний', 'adjective', 'This is a recent photo.', 'Bu yaqindagi surat.', 'ˈriːsnt'], ['decade', 'o‘n yillik', 'десятилетие', 'noun', 'He lived there for a decade.', 'U u yerda o‘n yil yashadi.', 'ˈdekeɪd'], ['whole', 'butun', 'целый', 'adjective', 'It rained the whole day.', 'Kun bo‘yi yomg‘ir yog‘di.', 'həʊl']],
      g: [['She has worked here ___ 2020.', 'since', 'for', 'ago', 'Boshlanish nuqtasi (2020) bilan “since”.'], ['We have been friends ___ ten years.', 'for', 'since', 'from', 'Muddat (ten years) bilan “for”.']],
      dlg: ['Teacher: How long have you studied English? Ali: I have studied it for four years. Teacher: And since when have you lived in this city? Ali: Since 2021. Teacher: So you have been here for a long time. Ali: Yes, for almost a decade of my life.', 'Since when has Ali lived in the city?', 'Since 2021', 'For four years', 'For a decade', 'He says “Since 2021”.'],
      rd: ['My grandfather has been a teacher for forty years. He has worked in the same school since 1985. He has taught thousands of students, and many of them still visit him. He hasn’t taken a long holiday for a decade, because he says that school is his second home. His family has asked him to retire, but he refuses.', ['How long has he been a teacher?', 'For forty years', 'Since 1980', 'For ten years'], ['He has worked in the same school since 1985.', 'True'], ['He wants to retire next year.', 'Not Given']],
      wr: ['Write 6 sentences about yourself with for and since (how long you have lived, studied, known someone).', 'for|since|have', 25, 'I have lived in this city since 2015. I have studied English for three years. I have known my best friend since school. We have been friends for ten years. My father has worked in a bank for twenty years.'],
